==================================================================
DAY 43 - PART B: LAB
Account safety, CLI tools, first look around
Time: 75-90 minutes
==================================================================

STEP 1: AWS account and MFA
---------------------------
1. Create an AWS account (or use your company's sandbox).
2. Turn on MFA for the root user. Don't use root day to day.
3. In IAM Identity Center (or IAM), create an admin user for
   yourself, with MFA. Use that from now on.


STEP 2: Budget alert (DO THIS NOW)
----------------------------------
AWS console -> Billing and Cost Management -> Budgets -> Create budget
  -> "Zero spend budget" AND a monthly cost budget of e.g. USD 20 with
  email alerts at 50% and 100%.
Also enable "Free tier usage alerts" in Billing preferences.


STEP 3: Install the AWS CLI v2
------------------------------
curl "https://awscli.amazonaws.com/awscli-exe-linux-x86_64.zip" -o awscliv2.zip
unzip -q awscliv2.zip && sudo ./aws/install
aws --version

Configure credentials (SSO recommended):
  aws configure sso          # if you use IAM Identity Center
  # or for an IAM user with access keys:
  aws configure              # region: ap-south-1, output: json
aws sts get-caller-identity  # who am I?


STEP 4: Install eksctl and helm
-------------------------------
ARCH=amd64
curl -sLO "https://github.com/eksctl-io/eksctl/releases/latest/download/eksctl_Linux_$ARCH.tar.gz"
tar -xzf eksctl_Linux_$ARCH.tar.gz -C /tmp && sudo install /tmp/eksctl /usr/local/bin/
eksctl version

curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/helm/helm/main/scripts/get-helm-3 | bash
helm version


STEP 5: Look at your default VPC and AZs
----------------------------------------
aws ec2 describe-availability-zones --query 'AvailabilityZones[].ZoneName' --output table
aws ec2 describe-vpcs --query 'Vpcs[].{ID:VpcId,CIDR:CidrBlock,Default:IsDefault}' --output table
aws ec2 describe-subnets --query 'Subnets[].{AZ:AvailabilityZone,CIDR:CidrBlock,Public:MapPublicIpOnLaunch}' --output table

(eksctl will create its own dedicated VPC with public + private
subnets in 2-3 AZs and a NAT gateway; you'll see it tomorrow.)


STEP 6: Check supported EKS versions and pricing
------------------------------------------------
Open the "Amazon EKS Kubernetes versions" page in the AWS docs:
  - pick a version in STANDARD support (versions in EXTENDED support
    cost about 6x more per hour for the control plane)
Open the EKS pricing page and the EC2 pricing page for t3.medium in
ap-south-1. Calculate the hourly cost of: 1 control plane + 2 x
t3.medium + 1 NAT gateway + 1 load balancer. Write it in Part C.


STEP 7: Write the cluster config (used tomorrow)
------------------------------------------------
mkdir -p ~/k8s-journey/cloud/eks && cd $_
vi cluster.yaml

apiVersion: eksctl.io/v1alpha5
kind: ClusterConfig
metadata:
  name: lab
  region: ap-south-1
  # version: "1.xx"     # optional; omit to use eksctl's default
iam:
  withOIDC: true
addons:
- name: vpc-cni
- name: coredns
- name: kube-proxy
- name: eks-pod-identity-agent
- name: aws-ebs-csi-driver
  wellKnownPolicies:
    ebsCSIController: true
managedNodeGroups:
- name: ng-1
  instanceType: t3.medium
  minSize: 1
  desiredCapacity: 2
  maxSize: 4
  volumeSize: 20
  privateNetworking: true
  iam:
    withAddonPolicies:
      autoScaler: true
      ebs: true

Read every line and write in Part C what it does.

eksctl create cluster -f cluster.yaml --dry-run | head -60

(--dry-run prints the full config with defaults, creates nothing.)


STEP 8: AKS / GKE equivalents (read)
------------------------------------
AKS:
  az login
  az group create -n lab-rg -l centralindia
  az aks create -g lab-rg -n lab --node-count 2 --node-vm-size Standard_B2s \
    --enable-oidc-issuer --enable-workload-identity --generate-ssh-keys
  az aks get-credentials -g lab-rg -n lab
  az group delete -n lab-rg --yes          # deletes EVERYTHING in the group
GKE:
  gcloud auth login ; gcloud config set project <PROJECT>
  gcloud container clusters create lab --region asia-south1 --num-nodes 1 \
    --machine-type e2-medium --workload-pool=<PROJECT>.svc.id.goog
  gcloud container clusters get-credentials lab --region asia-south1
  gcloud container clusters delete lab --region asia-south1

Commit:
  cd ~/k8s-journey && git add . && git commit -m "day43: cloud prep"
